              "text": "以为 (yǐwéi) is built from 以 'to take' and 为 'to make', both inherited from Middle Chinese, yiX and hjwe (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to use' and lists the second as the everyday spelling of a word glossed 'to make'. How the pair came to mean a belief that turns out wrong is not settled."
